{"availability":"available","full":"cobbler/cobbler","name":"cobbler","description":"Cobbler is a versatile Linux deployment server","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":2774,"forks":658,"created":"2011-11-08T15:01:00Z","updated":"2026-10-07T10:34:28Z","license":"GPL-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://cobbler.github.io","topics":["cobbler","deployment","dhcp","hacktoberfest","pxe","python","tftp"],"demo":"https://cobbler.github.io/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:36:45.356Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:36:45.356Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:36:45.356Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T03:36:45.356Z","stars":2774,"forks":658}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Cobbler is a Linux installation server that allows for rapid setup of network installation environments. It glues together and automates many associated Linux tasks so you do not have to hop between lots of various commands and applications when rolling out new systems, and, in some cases, changing existing ones. It can help with installation, DNS, DHCP, package updates, power management, configuration management orchestration, and much more.","To view the man-pages, install the RPM and run man cobbler or run perldoc cobbler.pod from a source checkout.","To build the RPM, run make rpms. Developers, try make webtest to do a local make install that preserves your configuration."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cobbler/cobbler/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a6449e3e8bf80eb991cac6b810ac1eaeffff14aee65e17872865fbdc965c34b6","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T03:36:45.513Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:36:45.513Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Cobbler is a Linux installation server that allows for rapid setup of network installation environments. It glues together and automates many associated Linux tasks so you do not have to hop between lots of various commands and applicati